s \"Indiana needs to revamp its child care system\". This shows the side that wants more support, so `direction-only`.\n  - **Mar 11, 2026:** he calls HEA 1177's employer credit a \"Small Step\" and backs a House Democratic proposal to release CCDF funds. Neither source shows his own vote, so `direction-only`.\n  - **Jan 15, 2026:** he criticizes the governor for putting child care off until next year. It names no policy clause, so `rhetorical`.\n- **Why blank:** his words put him on the side of more public support. They never say whether that support should reach every family, low- and middle-income families with provider grants, or families below an income threshold. Those are the clauses that separate rungs 1, 2 and 3.\n- **needs_source:**\n  - the House roll call and bill text for HEA 1177 (2026);\n  - the roll call and text for the Democratic amendment to SEA 4 on releasing CCDF funds;\n  - any childcare subsidy or provider-grant bill Pierce authored or co-sponsored.\n- **Quotes:**\n  - The \"revamp\" sentence is `direction` and quotable.\n  - The sentence about Republicans voting down the proposal is `none` and not quotable (`not-forward`).","ttft_ms":11829,"type":"result","duration_ms":32424,"uuid":"88bb63e6-2844-464c-8b89-1619c58e0b99","ttft_stream_ms":5269,"time_to_request_ms":59,"first_content_frame_ms":5270,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
